  "chapter": 671,
  "signer": "KATHY HOCHUL",
  "text": " \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 52 Chapter 671\n \n        MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 1069, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\n        prohibiting the lease of  state  forests,  reforestation  areas,\n        wildlife  management  areas  and  unique  areas  for gas and oil\n        production\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill would prohibit the leasing of state  forests,  reforestation\nareas,  wildlife  management  areas  and  unique  areas  for gas and oil\nproduction.\n \n  It is critical that we conserve state lands for future generations  to\nenjoy.  While  I understand the intent behind this bill, it could affect\nexisting leases and create a risk of  abandoned  or  improperly  plugged\nwells, burdening State taxpayers and jeopardizing pristine state lands.\n \n  I  have  reached an agreement with the Legislature to enact amendments\naddressing these issues. On the basis of this agreement, I am pleased to\nsign this bill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                         (signed) KATHY HOCHUL\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2025
 },
